I want to build a website for an architecture and interior design firm, with an admin panel.
Everything runs locally for now. The backend must expose a clean JSON REST API under /api
so a mobile app can reuse it later.

## Tech stack
- Backend: Python, FastAPI, PyMySQL (plain parameterized SQL, no ORM), python-dotenv, local MySQL
- Frontend: server-rendered pages with Jinja2 templates + vanilla JavaScript + CSS (no frameworks, no build step).
  Responsive and mobile-friendly.
- Admin auth: session cookie (HttpOnly) after login, passwords hashed with bcrypt, CSRF protection on admin forms
- Config in .env (never commit). Provide .env.example.

## Public website (no login)
Top navigation / home page with 5 sections:
1. Residential Interior Design
2. Commercial Interior Design
3. Bunglow Design
4. Apartment and Commercial Complex
5. Inquiry

Sections 1-4: each has its own page listing that category's projects. For each project show:
- Title first, e.g. "Padma Madhav, Kothrud (2 BHK)", "XYZ Park, Kothrud (Office)",
  "Sai Bunglow, Kothrud (Bunglow)", "Sai Complex, Kothrud (Complex)"
- Below the title, the project's images in an animated auto-sliding carousel (smooth fade/slide transition,
  prev/next arrows, dots, swipe support, pause on hover). Clicking an image opens a full-screen lightbox.
- Lazy-load images. Show a friendly message if a section has no projects yet.

Section 5 - Inquiry form (also a JSON endpoint POST /api/inquiries):
- Common fields: Name, Mobile No (10-digit validation), Email (format validation), Address
- Radio: "Interior" or "Bunglow/Apartment Design"

If "Interior" is selected, show:
  - House type (radio): 1 BHK, 2 BHK, 3 BHK, Bunglow, Other
    (if Other, show a text box to specify)
  - Budget (radio/dropdown): Under 5L, 5-10L, 10-20L, 20-50L, Above 50L

If "Bunglow/Apartment Design" is selected, show:
  - Area (number, in sq ft)
  - Upload Layout (file upload button): accepts JPG, PNG, PDF only, max 10 MB
  - Budget (same ranges as above)

Fields switch dynamically without page reload; only the visible section's fields are required and
submitted. Validate on both client and server (check file type by content, not only extension).
On submit save to MySQL, show a success message and reset the form.

## Admin panel (/admin)
- Login page (username + password). Seed one admin via a script using credentials from .env.
  No hardcoded passwords. Rate-limit login attempts.
- Add Project form: choose section (1-4), title, upload multiple images (JPG/PNG/WEBP, max 5 MB each,
  auto-generate sensible filenames, preview before upload)
- Manage Projects: list by section, edit title, add/remove/reorder images, delete project
- View Inquiries: table, newest first, filter by service type, click to view full details,
  download the uploaded layout file, delete inquiry
- Logout

## Data model
- admins (id, username, password_hash, created_at)
- projects (id, section_id, title, created_at)
- project_images (id, project_id, path, sort_order)
- inquiries (id, name, mobile, email, address, service_type [interior|bunglow_apartment],
  house_type nullable, house_type_other nullable, area_sqft nullable,
  layout_file_path nullable, budget_range, created_at)
- Create tables automatically on startup.

## Security / storage rules
- Project images: stored in /uploads/projects, publicly served.
- Inquiry layout files: stored in /uploads/layouts, NOT publicly served. Only logged-in admins can download them
  via a protected route. Randomized filenames.
- Use parameterized queries only, escape template output, validate everything, return proper error codes.
- Add .gitignore (Python, .env, venv, uploads/).

## Design
Clean, elegant, architectural look: white/off-white background, charcoal text, one warm accent colour,
generous spacing, a good serif + sans-serif font pairing (use local or system fonts, no external CDNs).

